@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Comment, CommentReport]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/CommentController.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/CommentResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/CommentPolicy.ts
+  - db/schema.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-code/fable-5-1", at: 2026-09-29T15:16:21.605Z }
+---
+
+# Hide comments at three distinct reports
+
+## Context
+
+Readers can comment under posts, and no moderator is on call. One bad
+actor must not be able to fill a post with spam, and one annoyed reader
+must not be able to remove a comment alone.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Any signed-in user may report a comment. `comment_reports` holds one
+  row per report, and a unique index on (`comment_id`, `user_id`) makes a
+  repeated report by the same user a no-op that still answers 204.
+- A comment with three or more reports (`COMMENT_HIDE_THRESHOLD` in
+  `app/Models/Comment.ts`) is left out of the post page for every
+  viewer, its author and the post's author included.
+- Hiding is derived from the report rows at read time
+  (`Comment.visibleOn()`); no flag or counter is stored on `comments`.
+- A hidden comment stays in `comments` so it can be reviewed later.
+- Deleting is a hard delete, allowed to the comment's author and to the
+  author of the post (`CommentPolicy.delete`). Deleting a post deletes
+  its comments and their reports.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The report rows are the single source of truth, so rows written by
+  review tooling count the same as rows written by the app.
+- The post page costs one grouped count per view on top of the comment
+  query.
+- There is no un-hide path and no review screen yet; both need a
+  follow-up decision. Until then a hidden comment can only be restored
+  by deleting report rows.
+- Three colluding accounts can hide any comment. Raising the threshold
+  is a one-constant change.
